# Project Structure

Use this folder structure consistently throughout the project.

```
src/
  pages/
  components/
  hooks/
  services/
  utils/
  assets/
  types/
```

## Pages

- All route-level components must be placed inside `src/pages`.
- Each page must have its own folder.
- Never place page components inside `src/components`.

```
src/pages/
  Home/
    Home.tsx
    Home.css
    index.ts
    components/
      Hero/
        Hero.tsx
        Hero.css
        index.ts
```

## Components

- Shared components used by multiple pages belong in `src/components`.
- Page-specific components belong in a `components` folder within that page.
- Every component must live in its own folder (see `03-component-structure.mdc`).

## Imports

- Import pages through their `index.ts`: `import { Home } from './pages/Home'`
- Import shared components through their `index.ts`: `import { Button } from './components/ui/Button'`
- Import page-specific components relative to the page or through their `index.ts`.

## Other Directories

- `hooks/` — custom React hooks
- `services/` — API clients and external service integrations
- `utils/` — pure utility functions
- `types/` — shared TypeScript types and interfaces
- `assets/` — static images, fonts, and media files
